plus 2 .gitignore fixes landed for lsp/ and mcp/).

## 3. Where to go next

- **The submenu.** Each repo has its own page sourced from its
  `openOODA/{repo}/docs/` directory.
- **The 26 capability tokens (20 implemented).** They appear across the LSP, MCP, and
  std visualisations. There is no ambient authority anywhere in the
  stack. (oodar v3.0.0 added the 26th token, `Metrics`, which
  re-uses the v2.1.0-reserved bit 0x800 for the cap-gated
  `oo_metrics_*` family. oodar v3.1.0 closed 4 round-4 fail-open
  CRITICALs found by the depth-first audit; v3.2.0 added a 56-row
  contract test for fail-closed on cap=0; v3.3.0 added the Rule 2
  bitmask subset check via `oo_cap_attenuate_v2`. The cap table
  is published at `oodar/sec/cap/cap_table.json` for lsp + oodac; north_star is 20.)
- **The polyrepo topology.** See `RULES.oot` §1.23 for the
  why behind the split.

## 4. Substrate home is oodar

**Actual state (2026-09-09):** `oodac/` has no `runtime/` tree.
Product build and `unique_fns` compile `oodar/oodar.c` plus a
host_rt TU (emit-tmp helpers and the Landlock jail ctor).
`ooda/` has no `runtime/` tree. The `oo_*` ABI lives in
`oodar/` (6 per-domain subdirs, 128 .c files, v4.0.7). `oo_slist_slice` and
`oo_sys_exec_wait` are real oodar symbols. `spawn`/`wait`/`kill`/
`epoll`/`inotify`/`prctl` refuse in oodar after a cap check.

The old cleanup chain (drop `chs_rt_*` from oodac, then delete
`ooda/runtime/`) is done. Do not re-add C shims under `oodac/`.

> The install command lives at the top and bottom of this page —
> it is the same component, not duplicated content.
